S5 working replacement pages. Population-level functional variant-composition and ALT-relative dosage summaries. Each point is one population;9core and10peripheral populations. Boxes show median and quartiles, whiskers extend to the most extreme value within1.5interquartile ranges; all populations shown. Panels contrast segregating-site ratios, exact hypergeometrically rarefied ratios, pooled ALT-copy ratios, mean individual ALT-copy ratios, homozygous-ALT ratios and summed per-site ALT-frequency ratios on a common call-rate mask. Segregating-site ratios exclude sites fixed within a population; other dosage summaries retain fixed ALT. All metrics are conditional on the supplied variant-only RAD panel, and do not establish ancestral state or fitness load.
Separate pages show strict predicted LOF (stop-gain and essential splice), all scored SIFT deleterious missense, and an explicitly documented SIFT quality sensitivity. SIFT unscored variants are excluded from prediction classes and coverage is tabulated. Synonymous denominators differ by metric and are reported in the supplementary tables; no invariant/callable-genome denominator is available. Population-class tests and uncertainty of mean differences are given in tables; figures show observed distributions without invented measurement error. Final placement/numbering pending.
